From 616a7607d1f790bc05d288918056ccd4a834681a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:36:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] advisors: the month's map scans in small kernels (B3
 A0, bit-identical)

The day-28 zone scan cost 2-25 ms for the same city: V8 optimized the
big scan functions on their first runs and threw the code away on rare
paths without type feedback, and on the per-call isZ closure (a new call
target on every scan). scanZones now calls fillZoneBlocks (the flood
fill) and classifyLots (the empty ready lots); lotFitAny's wide search
is lotFitWide, its rd closure the module-level roadAtXZ; scanOutages'
and scanRubble's rare branches are waterNeedMet / addOutage and
addRubble. Same operations in the same order, integer counts and cell
indices only.

tests/sim/exact/advisorsScan.test.ts compares the kernels' ZoneScan and
lotFitAt with a frozen copy of the base on random cities (odd tiles,
steep lots, outages, rubble, roadless blocks), with Object.is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KT9tXthEhyzExdUuGEecAJ
